characterization of spinal neuronal response properties on anaesthetized rats after ligation of spinal nerves L5&#x02013;L6</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>507</volume><fpage>881</fpage><lpage>894</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9508847</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>S-R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>H-L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hypersensitivity of spinothalamic tract neurons associated with diabetic neuropathic pain in rats</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>2726</fpage><lpage>2733</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12037174</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>BN</given-names></name><name><surname>Perl</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spinal neurons specifically excited by noxious or thermal stimuli: marginal zone of the dorsal horn</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>1969</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>293</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5415075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Craig</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Krout</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Andrew</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantitative response characteristics of thermoreceptive and nociceptive lamina I spinothalamic neurons in the cat</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>2001</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>1459</fpage><lpage>1480</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11535691</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Devor</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Centralization, central sensitization and neuropathic pain. Focus on &#x0201c;Sciatic chronic constriction injury produces cell-type-specific changes in the electrophysiological properties of rat substantia gelatinosa neurons&#x0201d;</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>522</fpage><lpage>523</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16835360</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feil</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Herbert</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Topographic organization of spinal and trigeminal sensory pathways to the rat parabrachial and K&#x000f6;lliker-Fuse nuclei</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><year>1995</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>506</fpage><lpage>528</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7759613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flecknell</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><source>Laboratory Animal Anaesthesia</source><year>1996</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Elsevier</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hara</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The anesthetic mechanisms of urethane: the effects on neurotransmitter-gated ion channels</article-title><source>Anesth Analg</source><year>2002</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>313</fpage><lpage>318</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11812690</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation